From 66205c2b0355217c785ef62c41335af8d4702446 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:44:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 105/106] Aurora: a menu over the paused game, and where frames
 wait

dol_aurora_set_hold_redraw(true): while the host holds the guest at a
present, the hold loop keeps presenting the last picture with the host
overlay drawn over it, so an ImGui menu that pauses the game stays live
(before, the hold only slept).

For finding the places that miss 60: DolAuroraFrameTiming counts the frames
shown (in-between frames included) and the in-between frames' totals (game
frames seen and interpolated, draws, rejected, unmatched), from
aurora_get_shown_frames and aurora_get_frame_interp_totals. A render worker
item or a drawable acquire or present that takes 60 ms or more is logged
([render-slow], DOL_RENDER_SLOW_MS), a GX batch of 100 ms or more logs its
first bytes ([gx-slow-bytes]), and DOL_GX_STALL_STACKS=1 has the translation
and render workers write their stacks when a batch runs 200 ms.
